- name: note_0
  id: note
  parameters:
    alias: ''
    comment: 'GENERAL SETUP:

      * In the File Source block, select the desired file. NOTE: This

      should be a file representing a simple 2D array of 8-bit

      integers, which themselves represent a grayscale image.

      * Set the image width manually using the "image_width"

      variable above. For example, if the image is 850 pixels wide,

      set the value in this variable block to 850.

      * If desired, set the dynamic range using the "dr" variable

      above.


      IF OUTPUTTING TO A SDR:

      * In the File Source, set the "Repeat" value to "Yes".

      * Connect the SDR sink to the output of the "Vector to Stream"

      block and disable / delete the "Throttle" block.

      * Set the desired sample rate above.

      * Set your desired sample rate using the "samp_rate" variable.


      IF OUTPUTTING TO A WAV FILE:

      * In the File Source, set the "Repeat" value to "No".

      * Enable the "Complex to Float" and "WAV File Sink" blocks.

      * In the WAV File Sink block, set the output filename with

      the extension ".wav".'
    note: General Instructions
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [40, 328.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
